{
  "_doc": "Test tiers, see TESTING.md. smoke: always run by npm run check and PR CI (one quick scenario per main feature). areas: feature areas, each with the files that belong to it (globs, source and scenario specs) and a hand-picked group of scenarios that runs whole when a change touches one of them; broad: the same for changes no area holds. limits: seconds of scenario time for a group beside smoke (area), for smoke, and for smoke with the three largest groups (local). perf: the files the perf benchmarks run (CI's perf job runs only when a change touches one). manual: left out of every default run, run them by name. known: checks failing on main that are tracked elsewhere; their FAIL lines are reported but don't fail a run (remove the entry with the fix).",
